{
    "1": {
        "reproduce_code": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <title>Reproduce Boundary Event Copy Bug</title>\n  <style>\n    #canvas { width: 100%; height: 100vh; border: 1px solid #ccc; }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <div id=\"canvas\"></div>\n\n  <!-- bpmn-js modeler from unpkg -->\n  <script src=\"https://unpkg.com/bpmn-js@8.4.0/dist/bpmn-modeler.development.js\"></script>\n  <script>\n    (function() {\n      var BpmnModeler = window.BpmnJS;\n\n      // Create the modeler instance\n      var modeler = new BpmnModeler({\n        container: '#canvas'\n      });\n\n      // Minimal BPMN XML with a Task and a Boundary Event\n      var xml = '<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>' +\n        '<definitions xmlns=\"http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL\" ' +\n                     'xmlns:bpmndi=\"http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI\" ' +\n                     'xmlns:dc=\"http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC\" ' +\n                     'id=\"Definitions_1\" targetNamespace=\"http://bpmn.io/schema/bpmn\">' +\n          '<process id=\"Process_1\" isExecutable=\"false\">' +\n            '<task id=\"Task_1\" name=\"My Task\" />' +\n            '<boundaryEvent id=\"BoundaryEvent_1\" attachedToRef=\"Task_1\" name=\"Error?\" />' +\n          '</process>' +\n          '<bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id=\"BPMNDiagram_1\">' +\n            '<bpmndi:BPMNPlane id=\"BPMNPlane_1\" bpmnElement=\"Process_1\">' +\n              '<bpmndi:BPMNShape id=\"Task_1_di\" bpmnElement=\"Task_1\">' +\n                '<dc:Bounds x=\"200\" y=\"200\" width=\"100\" height=\"80\" />' +\n              '</bpmndi:BPMNShape>' +\n              '<bpmndi:BPMNShape id=\"BoundaryEvent_1_di\" bpmnElement=\"BoundaryEvent_1\">' +\n                '<dc:Bounds x=\"295\" y=\"260\" width=\"36\" height=\"36\" />' +\n              '</bpmndi:BPMNShape>' +\n            '</bpmndi:BPMNPlane>' +\n          '</bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>' +\n        '</definitions>';\n\n      // Import and immediately perform copy/paste\n      modeler.importXML(xml).then(function() {\n        var elementRegistry = modeler.get('elementRegistry');\n        var copyPaste = modeler.get('copyPaste');\n\n        // Look up the two elements\n        var task = elementRegistry.get('Task_1');\n        var boundary = elementRegistry.get('BoundaryEvent_1');\n\n        // Programmatically copy both\n        copyPaste.copy([ task, boundary ]);\n\n        // Paste with an offset (200px to the right)\n        copyPaste.paste({ delta: { x: 200, y: 0 } });\n      }).catch(function(err) {\n        console.error('Import error:', err);\n      });\n    })();\n  </script>\n</body>\n</html>",
        "explanation": "1. We define a minimal BPMN XML containing a single Task (Task_1) and a Boundary Event (BoundaryEvent_1) that references Task_1 via its attachedToRef attribute and corresponding DI shapes with positions.\n2. After importing the XML into a bpmn-js Modeler, we use the built-in copyPaste service to copy both the Task element and its Boundary Event.\n3. We then paste the copied elements at an X-offset of 200 pixels.\n\nExpected outcome: the pasted Boundary Event would be re-attached to the pasted Task. Actual outcome (bug): the pasted Boundary Event appears unconnected, demonstrating that the boundary attachment relationship is not preserved on copy/paste.",
        "bug_scenario": "In the reproduced scenario we start with a simple BPMN diagram containing a single Task (Task_1) and a Boundary Event (BoundaryEvent_1) attached to that Task.  Immediately after import we programmatically copy both the Task and its Boundary Event and paste them at an offset of +200px in X.  What you will see is that the Task copy is placed correctly, but the copied Boundary Event is no longer attached\u2014it floats by itself instead of snapping to the new Task instance."
    }
}